  "status": "Approved",
  "description": "Application for the following works to St John of Jerusalem Church, a Grade II* listed active church located on Lauriston Road, Hackney.\n1. Graded access into the church to improve accessibility\n2. Two air source heat pump unit enclosures to the church perimeter to supply heating to modernised transept rooms to the north and east elevations, positioned to minimise visual impact\n3. Vents and flues to aid the working of the air source heat pump, new WCs in the modernised transept rooms and commercial kitchen in the old vestry.\n4. Electric radiant heaters and associated electrical items.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "Any new plant shall be installed, together with any associated ancillary equipment, so as to prevent the transmission of noise and vibration into neighbouring premises. The rated noise level from all plant and ancillary equipment shall not increase the existing background noise level (10dB below) when measured 1m external from the nearest residential or noise sensitive premises.REASON: To protect acceptable local noise levels"
  ],
